Package: pkident
Title: Structural and Practical Identifiability for Pharmacokinetic and Pharmacodynamic Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Daiki", "Kumakura", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "55353329+DaikiKumakura@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Determines which parameters of pharmacokinetic and pharmacodynamic
    ordinary differential equation models written in 'rxode2' can be
    identified. Structural identifiability (which parameters and which
    combinations can be determined from the observed outputs and known doses)
    is decided by two independent methods that must agree. Practical
    identifiability gives the expected precision of each parameter for a
    sampling design and compares designs. Likelihood profiles of 'nlmixr2'
    fits are classified as bounded, one-sided, flat or shallow and linked to
    the structural result. Decisions are local and are stated as such.
